.\" Generated from the goobers command registry — do not edit by hand.
.TH "GOOBERS FIX" "1" "" "Goobers" "Goobers Manual"
.SH NAME
goobers fix \- mechanically migrate workflows to a target dslVersion, one step at a time (DVL-6)
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBgoobers fix\fR [\fIoptions\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.nf
Usage: goobers fix (--to <version> | --instance-schema | --rollback) [--write] [--allow-policy-expansion] [path]

Exactly one mode is required per invocation.

--to <version> mechanically migrates workflows; --instance-schema repairs
instance.yaml's schema revision. They are separate remedies over separate
files, so they are never combined in one run.

Mechanically migrate every workflow under an instance root (default path
".") from its current dslVersion to <version>, one registered version
step at a time (DVL-6). Prints a reviewable unified diff per changed
workflow file by default; --write applies the diff to each file in
place instead. Refuses a workflow that is already at <version>, and
refuses any jump for which no direct one-step migration is registered —
chain multiple `fix` invocations for a multi-step upgrade, never a
silent multi-step rewrite. Never runs automatically; this is always an
author-run, reviewable change. Exit codes: 0 = migrated (or nothing to
migrate), 1 = one or more workflows could not be migrated,
2 = usage/IO error.

DSL 2.0 to 2.1 is an opt-in PREVIEW migration. Watcher comment-on-issue
additions are listed in the diff; --write requires --allow-policy-expansion
when new actions are added. The diff also includes each Workflow's required
metadata.annotations goobers.dev/allow-preview-features: "true" opt-in.
--to 2.1 --write accepts this displayed preview target. Authored opt-outs
are refused; Instance/Gaggle settings stay unchanged.
2.1 writes save one bounded .dsl21-migration-backup.json outside config.
--rollback restores its original bytes, refusing modified destinations.
After acceptance, archive/remove that backup before another migration.

--instance-schema is the one-line remedy for the instance.yaml load
refusal "runners: requires schemaVersion 2" (#4217): a config that
declares a runners: inventory must also declare the schema revision that
introduced it, so an older binary refuses the file outright instead of
loading it and silently dropping the whole inventory. It inserts
"schemaVersion: 2" after the apiVersion:/kind: header and changes
nothing else — comments, ordering and formatting survive byte for byte,
because this repairs a file the strict loader currently refuses to parse.
A schemaVersion line that is present but wrong is reported, never
rewritten: that is a deliberate operator value, not an omission. Prints a
diff by default; --write applies it. Cannot be combined with --to.
.fi
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
goobers fix --to 2.0
goobers fix --to 2.0 --write ./instance
goobers fix --instance-schema --write ./instance
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
\fBgoobers\fR(1)
